# ThousandEyes MCP Lab

- Static single-page site in `site/` (generated from `src/shell.html` by `python3 src/build.py`), scoreboard and onboarding API in `api/` (AWS SAM, Python 3.12 Lambda, DynamoDB, SSM), hosting in `infra/` (S3 + CloudFront, optional custom domain), one-shot deploy in `scripts/deploy.sh`. Offline tests and a no-AWS dev server in `api/tests/` (`make test`, `make dev`).
- Full map, rules and verification steps: `AGENTS.md`. Deployment runbook: `DEPLOY.md`. The owner's task for you: `CURSOR_PROMPT.md`.

## Hard rules

- Never commit secrets. `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and `PROCTOR_KEY` go in as env vars to `scripts/deploy.sh`; `samconfig.toml` stays git-ignored. The ThousandEyes token is entered on the `#proctor` page and lives only in SSM Parameter Store: no route returns it, nothing logs it.
- Accepted answers live only in `api/answers.json`, which is git-ignored and must never be committed; the deploy passes them to the Lambda as a NoEcho parameter and the page carries SHA-256 hashes. If the file is missing, ask the owner for it.
- `canon()` in `api/app.py` and in `src/shell.html` must stay byte-for-byte equivalent in behaviour.
- `site/index.html` is generated: edit the source and rebuild, commit both.
- Cisco dark brand: Midnight `#07182D`, white text, Cisco Blue `#02C8FF` headings, Medium Blue `#0A60FF` outlines, Magenta `#FF007F` and Orange `#FF9000` decorative only, outlined containers, no fills. No em dashes in any text. Australian spelling.
- Onboarding writes into the owner's ThousandEyes organisation: keep every gate (sign-up switch, event code, cap, one record per email, proctor key on all `/proctor` routes). Test against `api/tests/fakes.py`, not the real organisation.
- Ask before: changing the domain, enabling the front desk (`/ask`), changing questions or scoring, deleting stacks.

## Deploy in one line

`AWS_REGION=ap-southeast-2 PROCTOR_KEY=... scripts/deploy.sh` with `api/answers.json` in place (add `DOMAIN`, `CERT_ARN`, `HOSTED_ZONE_ID`, `EVENT_NAME`, `EVENT_DATE`, `EVENT_CITY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` as needed; pass the same `PROCTOR_KEY` on every deploy), then `scripts/smoke.sh`. Use the script, never `sam deploy --guided`.
